    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests jogging back and forth between two elements over the begin/end boundary of the list. <p>Cursor notation used in comments: {@code ^} marks the cursor position within the list. For example, {@code [^a b]} means the cursor is before \"a\" (at index 0); {@code [a^b]} means the cursor is between \"a\" and \"b\" (at index 1); {@code [ab^]} means the cursor is past the end (at index 2). Because the iterator loops, {@code [ab^]} and {@code [^a b]} behave identically for the next navigation call.</p>"
   },
   {
    "id": "i2",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     25,
     25
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Cursor starts at the beginning of the list: [^a b]"
   },
   {
    "id": "i3",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     28,
     29
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "previous() at the begin boundary wraps to the last element. Returns \"b\" and leaves cursor between \"a\" and \"b\": [a^b]"
   },
   {
    "id": "i4",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     32,
     32
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "next() at [a^b] advances past \"b\", reaching the end: [ab^]"
   },
   {
    "id": "i5",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     35,
     35
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "previous() at the end boundary [ab^] steps back to \"b\": [a^b]"
   },
   {
